<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charSet="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/><link rel="preload" as="image" href="/images/ThePoolLab.png"/><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_next/static/css/d071dca61fbb01bf.css" crossorigin="" data-precedence="next"/><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_next/static/css/0fc6c400c3ed5371.css" crossorigin="" data-precedence="next"/><link rel="preload" as="script" fetchPriority="low" href="/_next/static/chunks/webpack-9104c05f1a1687bc.js" crossorigin=""/><script src="/_next/static/chunks/fd9d1056-4dbbcf07a05c3f48.js" async="" crossorigin=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/472-6eced84fcf03e6a3.js" async="" crossorigin=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/main-app-ce281d8555633725.js" async="" crossorigin=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/326-bff252670b7455ef.js" async=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/app/blog/%5Bslug%5D/page-23a4c3f098b125a3.js" async=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/975-95592eb349967368.js" async=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/app/layout-4ee2f436a51b65f2.js" async=""></script><title>Dolphin Nautilus Titan vs Polaris 9650iQ Sport: Which Premium Robotic Pool Cleaner Is Better in 2026? - The Pool Lab</title><meta name="description" content="Compare the Dolphin Nautilus Titan and Polaris 9650iQ Sport across cleaning performance, navigation, smart features, filtration, wall climbing, and long-term value to determine which robotic pool cleaner is best for your pool."/><link rel="canonical" href="https://www.the-pool-lab.com/blog/dolphin-nautilus-titan-vs-polaris-9650iq-sport"/><meta property="og:title" content="Dolphin Nautilus Titan vs Polaris 9650iQ Sport: Which Premium Robotic Pool Cleaner Is Better in 2026?"/><meta property="og:description" content="Compare the Dolphin Nautilus Titan and Polaris 9650iQ Sport across cleaning performance, navigation, smart features, filtration, wall climbing, and long-term value to determine which robotic pool cleaner is best for your pool."/><meta property="og:type" content="article"/><meta property="article:published_time" content="2026-06-03"/><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"/><meta name="twitter:title" content="The Pool Lab - Your ultimate guide to Robot Pool Cleaners, reviews, and maintenance tips."/><meta name="twitter:description" content="Your ultimate guide to Robot Pool Cleaners, reviews, and maintenance tips."/><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://www.the-pool-lab.com/images/ThePoolLabOG.png"/><script src="/_next/static/chunks/polyfills-c67a75d1b6f99dc8.js" crossorigin="" noModule=""></script></head><body class="d-flex flex-column min-vh-100"><nav class="navbar navbar-expand-lg navbar-light bg-light"><div class="container"><a class="navbar-brand d-flex align-items-center" href="/"><div style="width:160px;height:90px;position:relative;margin-right:10px"><img src="/images/ThePoolLab.png" alt="The Pool Lab Logo" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:contain"/></div><span class="d-none d-sm-inline">The Pool Lab</span></a><button class="navbar-toggler" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#navbarNav"><span class="navbar-toggler-icon"></span></button><div class="collapse navbar-collapse" id="navbarNav"><ul class="navbar-nav ms-auto"><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/">Home</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/reviews">Reviews</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/best-of">Best of</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/guides">Guides</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/about">About</a></li></ul></div></div></nav><main class="flex-grow-1"><div class="container my-5"><nav aria-label="breadcrumb"><ol class="breadcrumb"><li class="breadcrumb-item"><a href="/">Home</a></li><li class="breadcrumb-item active" aria-current="page">Blog</li></ol></nav><article><h1 class="mb-4">Dolphin Nautilus Titan vs Polaris 9650iQ Sport: Which Premium Robotic Pool Cleaner Is Better in 2026?</h1><p class="text-muted mb-5">Posted on <!-- -->2026-06-03</p><div class="row"><div class="col-lg-8"><div><h2>Quick Verdict</h2><p>The <strong>Dolphin Nautilus Titan</strong> and <strong>Polaris 9650iQ Sport</strong> are both premium robotic pool cleaners designed for pool owners who want more than basic cleaning performance.</p><p>The <strong>Nautilus Titan</strong> focuses on simplicity, Wi-Fi connectivity, easy maintenance, and strong all-around cleaning. It delivers a modern ownership experience while maintaining Dolphin's reputation for reliability.</p><p>The <strong>Polaris 9650iQ Sport</strong> emphasizes advanced navigation, premium mobility, app-based controls, and a more feature-rich experience. It is often considered one of Polaris' flagship robotic pool cleaners.</p><p>If you want the best balance of cleaning performance and ease of ownership, choose the Titan. If you want maximum features and advanced mobility, choose the Polaris.</p><h2>At-a-Glance Comparison</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Nautilus Titan</th><th>Polaris 9650iQ Sport</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Best For</td><td>Balanced performance and convenience</td><td>Premium features and navigation</td></tr><tr><td>Wi-Fi Connectivity</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>App Control</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Wall Climbing</td><td>Excellent</td><td>Excellent</td></tr><tr><td>Waterline Cleaning</td><td>Very Good</td><td>Excellent</td></tr><tr><td>Navigation</td><td>Very Good</td><td>Excellent</td></tr><tr><td>Ease of Ownership</td><td>Excellent</td><td>Very Good</td></tr><tr><td>Value</td><td>Excellent</td><td>Good</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Cleaning Performance</h2><p>Both robots deliver excellent cleaning results in residential pools. They effectively remove leaves, dirt, bugs, pollen, and other common debris while cleaning floors and walls.</p><p>The Titan delivers strong cleaning performance through efficient navigation and proven Dolphin scrubbing technology. It is particularly appealing because it combines premium features with straightforward operation.</p><p>The Polaris 9650iQ Sport uses a four-wheel-drive mobility system that helps it navigate drains, slopes, and complex pool geometries. In difficult pools, it often demonstrates slightly better coverage consistency.</p><p>Winner: <strong>Polaris 9650iQ Sport</strong>, by a small margin.</p><h2>Navigation and Coverage</h2><p>Navigation becomes increasingly important as pools become larger or more complex.</p><p>The Nautilus Titan uses Dolphin's scanning and route-planning technologies to achieve efficient coverage. Most owners will find its cleaning patterns more than sufficient.</p><p>The Polaris 9650iQ Sport is widely regarded as one of the strongest navigators in the category. Its mobility system helps it maintain traction and coverage even in pools with unusual layouts.</p><p>Winner: <strong>Polaris 9650iQ Sport</strong>.</p><h2>Smart Features and Connectivity</h2><p>Both cleaners support smartphone connectivity and remote scheduling.</p><p>The Titan uses the MyDolphin Plus app, allowing owners to schedule cleanings, start cycles remotely, and monitor operation.</p><p>The Polaris 9650iQ Sport provides similar functionality through Polaris' connected platform while adding additional control options and customization.</p><p>The differences are relatively minor in everyday use.</p><p>Winner: <strong>Tie</strong>.</p><h2>Filtration and Debris Handling</h2><p>Both cleaners handle common residential debris effectively.</p><p>The Titan's large top-loading basket is easy to remove and clean. It performs especially well with mixed debris loads and routine maintenance cleaning.</p><p>The Polaris features a large debris canister that excels with larger debris and leaf-heavy environments.</p><p>Most owners will be satisfied with either system, though Polaris gains a small advantage when debris loads become heavy.</p><p>Winner: <strong>Polaris 9650iQ Sport</strong>.</p><h2>Wall Climbing and Waterline Cleaning</h2><p>Wall climbing performance is excellent on both robots.</p><p>The Titan consistently climbs walls and provides strong waterline coverage in most pools.</p><p>The Polaris often spends more time actively cleaning the waterline and tends to feel more confident on complex surfaces because of its drive system.</p><p>Winner: <strong>Polaris 9650iQ Sport</strong>.</p><h2>Ease of Ownership</h2><p>This is where the Titan shines.</p><p>The lighter chassis, simple maintenance, intuitive controls, and user-friendly app make the cleaner exceptionally easy to live with.</p><p>The Polaris provides more features but also introduces additional complexity. Owners who enjoy technology may appreciate the flexibility, while others may prefer the Titan's simplicity.</p><p>Winner: <strong>Nautilus Titan</strong>.</p><h2>Long-Term Value</h2><p>The Nautilus Titan generally delivers a stronger value proposition because it provides premium cleaning performance while often costing less than the Polaris 9650iQ Sport.</p><p>The Polaris justifies its higher pricing through advanced navigation, mobility, and additional premium features.</p><p>Whether those upgrades are worthwhile depends on your pool and priorities.</p><p>Winner: <strong>Nautilus Titan</strong>.</p><h2>Who Should Buy the Nautilus Titan?</h2><ul><li>Buyers who want premium performance without overpaying.</li><li>Pool owners who value simplicity.</li><li>Users who want app control and scheduling.</li><li>Owners focused on long-term value.</li><li>Anyone seeking a balanced premium cleaner.</li></ul><h2>Who Should Buy the Polaris 9650iQ Sport?</h2><ul><li>Owners of complex pool layouts.</li><li>Buyers who want advanced navigation.</li><li>Pools with significant obstacles or slopes.</li><li>Technology-focused owners.</li><li>Users who want Polaris' flagship experience.</li></ul><h2>Final Recommendation</h2><p>For most pool owners, the <strong>Dolphin Nautilus Titan</strong> offers the better balance of price, cleaning performance, convenience, and long-term value.</p><p>The <strong>Polaris 9650iQ Sport</strong> remains an excellent premium cleaner and may be the better choice for pools with complex layouts where advanced mobility and navigation provide meaningful benefits.</p><p>If you want the smarter overall purchase, choose the Titan. If you want the most advanced Polaris robotic cleaner, choose the 9650iQ Sport.</p><h2>Related Resources</h2><ul><li><a href='/reviews/Dolphin-Nautilus-Titan'>Dolphin Nautilus Titan Review</a></li><li><a href='/reviews/Polaris-9650iQ-Sport'>Polaris 9650iQ Sport Review</a></li><li><a href='/blog/polaris-vs-dolphin-robotic-pool-cleaners'>Polaris vs Dolphin</a></li><li><a href='/blog/dolphin-nautilus-cc-plus-vs-nautilus-titan'>Nautilus CC Plus vs Nautilus Titan</a></li><li><a href='/blog/dolphin-premier-vs-polaris-9650iq-sport'>Dolphin Premier vs Polaris 9650iQ Sport</a></li></ul><h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2><h3>Which cleaner has better navigation?</h3><p>The Polaris 9650iQ Sport generally offers stronger navigation and mobility, particularly in complex pools.</p><h3>Is the Nautilus Titan worth buying over the Polaris?</h3><p>For many pool owners, yes. The Titan offers excellent cleaning performance, smart features, and strong value at a lower price point.</p><h3>Do both cleaners support smartphone control?</h3><p>Yes. Both models provide app connectivity, scheduling, and remote operation.</p><h3>Which cleaner is easier to maintain?</h3><p>The Nautilus Titan is generally easier to maintain because of its lightweight design and straightforward filtration system.</p><h3>Which model should most pool owners choose?</h3><p>Most pool owners will be best served by the Nautilus Titan, while buyers with complex pools may benefit from the Polaris 9650iQ Sport's advanced navigation capabilities.</p></div><div class="mt-5"><a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="/reviews">Find Your Perfect Robot</a></div></div></div></article></div></main><footer class="bg-dark text-white text-center py-3 mt-auto"><div class="container"><p class="mb-1">© <!-- -->2026<!-- --> <!-- -->The Pool Lab<!-- -->. All rights reserved.</p><small class="text-white-50">The Pool Lab<!-- --> is a participant in the Amazon Services LLC Associates Program, an affiliate advertising program designed to provide a means for sites to earn advertising fees by advertising and linking to Amazon.com.</small></div></footer><script src="/_next/static/chunks/webpack-9104c05f1a1687bc.js" crossorigin="" async=""></script><script>(self.__next_f=self.__next_f||[]).push([0]);self.__next_f.push([2,null])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1:HL[\"/_next/static/css/d071dca61fbb01bf.css\",\"style\",{\"crossOrigin\":\"\"}]\n2:HL[\"/_next/static/css/0fc6c400c3ed5371.css\",\"style\",{\"crossOrigin\":\"\"}]\n0:\"$L3\"\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"4:I[3728,[],\"\"]\n6:I[9928,[],\"\"]\n7:I[8326,[\"326\",\"static/chunks/326-bff252670b7455ef.js\",\"308\",\"static/chunks/app/blog/%5Bslug%5D/page-23a4c3f098b125a3.js\"],\"\"]\n8:I[6954,[],\"\"]\n9:I[7264,[],\"\"]\nc:I[5826,[\"326\",\"static/chunks/326-bff252670b7455ef.js\",\"308\",\"static/chunks/app/blog/%5Bslug%5D/page-23a4c3f098b125a3.js\"],\"\"]\nd:I[7625,[\"326\",\"static/chunks/326-bff252670b7455ef.js\",\"975\",\"static/chunks/975-95592eb349967368.js\",\"185\",\"static/chunks/app/layout-4ee2f436a51b65f2.js\"],\"\"]\ne:I[6507,[\"326\",\"static/chunks/3"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"26-bff252670b7455ef.js\",\"975\",\"static/chunks/975-95592eb349967368.js\",\"185\",\"static/chunks/app/layout-4ee2f436a51b65f2.js\"],\"\"]\nb:T1e4f,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"\u003ch2\u003eQuick Verdict\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe \u003cstrong\u003eDolphin Nautilus Titan\u003c/strong\u003e and \u003cstrong\u003ePolaris 9650iQ Sport\u003c/strong\u003e are both premium robotic pool cleaners designed for pool owners who want more than basic cleaning performance.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe \u003cstrong\u003eNautilus Titan\u003c/strong\u003e focuses on simplicity, Wi-Fi connectivity, easy maintenance, and strong all-around cleaning. It delivers a modern ownership experience while maintaining Dolphin's reputation for reliability.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe \u003cstrong\u003ePolaris 9650iQ Sport\u003c/strong\u003e emphasizes advanced navigation, premium mobility, app-based controls, and a more feature-rich experience. It is often considered one of Polaris' flagship robotic pool cleaners.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf you want the best balance of cleaning performance and ease of ownership, choose the Titan. If you want maximum features and advanced mobility, choose the Polaris.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eAt-a-Glance Comparison\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ctable\u003e\u003cthead\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003cth\u003eCategory\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eNautilus Titan\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003ePolaris 9650iQ Sport\u003c/th\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/thead\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eBest For\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eBalanced performance and convenience\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003ePremium features and navigation\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eWi-Fi Connectivity\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eYes\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eYes\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eApp Control\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eYes\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eYes\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eWall Climbing\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eExcellent\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eExcellent\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eWaterline Cleaning\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eVery Good\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eExcellent\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eNavigation\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eVery Good\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eExcellent\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eEase of Ownership\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eExcellent\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eVery Good\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eValue\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eExcellent\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eGood\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003ch2\u003eCleaning Performance\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eBoth robots deliver excellent cleaning results in residential pools. They effectively remove leaves, dirt, bugs, pollen, and other common debris while cleaning floors and walls.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Titan delivers strong cleaning performance through efficient navigation and proven Dolphin scrubbing technology. It is particularly appealing because it combines premium features with straightforward operation.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Polaris 9650iQ Sport uses a four-wheel-drive mobility system that helps it navigate drains, slopes, and complex pool geometries. In difficult pools, it often demonstrates slightly better coverage consistency.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWinner: \u003cstrong\u003ePolaris 9650iQ Sport\u003c/strong\u003e, by a small margin.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eNavigation and Coverage\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eNavigation becomes increasingly important as pools become larger or more complex.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Nautilus Titan uses Dolphin's scanning and route-planning technologies to achieve efficient coverage. Most owners will find its cleaning patterns more than sufficient.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Polaris 9650iQ Sport is widely regarded as one of the strongest navigators in the category. Its mobility system helps it maintain traction and coverage even in pools with unusual layouts.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWinner: \u003cstrong\u003ePolaris 9650iQ Sport\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eSmart Features and Connectivity\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eBoth cleaners support smartphone connectivity and remote scheduling.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Titan uses the MyDolphin Plus app, allowing owners to schedule cleanings, start cycles remotely, and monitor operation.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Polaris 9650iQ Sport provides similar functionality through Polaris' connected platform while adding additional control options and customization.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe differences are relatively minor in everyday use.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWinner: \u003cstrong\u003eTie\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eFiltration and Debris Handling\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eBoth cleaners handle common residential debris effectively.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Titan's large top-loading basket is easy to remove and clean. It performs especially well with mixed debris loads and routine maintenance cleaning.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Polaris features a large debris canister that excels with larger debris and leaf-heavy environments.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eMost owners will be satisfied with either system, though Polaris gains a small advantage when debris loads become heavy.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWinner: \u003cstrong\u003ePolaris 9650iQ Sport\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eWall Climbing and Waterline Cleaning\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eWall climbing performance is excellent on both robots.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Titan consistently climbs walls and provides strong waterline coverage in most pools.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Polaris often spends more time actively cleaning the waterline and tends to feel more confident on complex surfaces because of its drive system.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWinner: \u003cstrong\u003ePolaris 9650iQ Sport\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eEase of Ownership\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eThis is where the Titan shines.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe lighter chassis, simple maintenance, intuitive controls, and user-friendly app make the cleaner exceptionally easy to live with.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Polaris provides more features but also introduces additional complexity. Owners who enjoy technology may appreciate the flexibility, while others may prefer the Titan's simplicity.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWinner: \u003cstrong\u003eNautilus Titan\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eLong-Term Value\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Nautilus Titan generally delivers a stronger value proposition because it provides premium cleaning performance while often costing less than the Polaris 9650iQ Sport.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Polaris justifies its higher pricing through advanced navigation, mobility, and additional premium features.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWhether those upgrades are worthwhile depends on your pool and priorities.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWinner: \u003cstrong\u003eNautilus Titan\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eWho Should Buy the Nautilus Titan?\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eBuyers who want premium performance without overpaying.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ePool owners who value simplicity.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eUsers who want app control and scheduling.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eOwners focused on long-term value.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eAnyone seeking a balanced premium cleaner.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003ch2\u003eWho Should Buy the Polaris 9650iQ Sport?\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eOwners of complex pool layouts.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eBuyers who want advanced navigation.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ePools with significant obstacles or slopes.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eTechnology-focused owners.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eUsers who want Polaris' flagship experience.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003ch2\u003eFinal Recommendation\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eFor most pool owners, the \u003cstrong\u003eDolphin Nautilus Titan\u003c/strong\u003e offers the better balance of price, cleaning performance, convenience, and long-term value.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe \u003cstrong\u003ePolaris 9650iQ Sport\u003c/strong\u003e remains an excellent premium cleaner and may be the better choice for pools with complex layouts where advanced mobility and navigation provide meaningful benefits.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf you want the smarter overall purchase, choose the Titan. If you want the most advanced Polaris robotic cleaner, choose the 9650iQ Sport.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eRelated Resources\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href='/reviews/Dolphin-Nautilus-Titan'\u003eDolphin Nautilus Titan Review\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href='/reviews/Polaris-9650iQ-Sport'\u003ePolaris 9650iQ Sport Review\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href='/blog/polaris-vs-dolphin-robotic-pool-cleaners'\u003ePolaris vs Dolphin\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href='/blog/dolphin-nautilus-cc-plus-vs-nautilus-titan'\u003eNautilus CC Plus vs Nautilus Titan\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href='/blog/dolphin-premier-vs-polaris-9650iq-sport'\u003eDolphin Premier vs Polaris 9650iQ Sport\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003ch2\u003eFrequently Asked Questions\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ch3\u003eWhich cleaner has better navigation?\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Polaris 9650iQ Sport generally offers stronger navigation and mobility, particularly in complex pools.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eIs the Nautilus Titan worth buying over the Polaris?\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eFor many pool owners, yes. The Titan offers excellent cleaning performance, smart features, and strong value at a lower price point.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eDo both cleaners support smartphone control?\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eYes. Both models provide app connectivity, scheduling, and remote operation.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eWhich cleaner is easier to maintain?\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Nautilus Titan is generally easier to maintain because of its lightweight design and straightforward filtration system.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eWhich model should most pool owners choose?\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eMost pool owners will be best served by the Nautilus Titan, while buyers with complex pools may benefit from the Polaris 9650iQ Sport's advanced navigation capabilities.\u003c/p\u003e"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"3:[[[\"$\",\"link\",\"0\",{\"rel\":\"stylesheet\",\"href\":\"/_next/static/css/d071dca61fbb01bf.css\",\"precedence\":\"next\",\"crossOrigin\":\"\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"1\",{\"rel\":\"stylesheet\",\"href\":\"/_next/static/css/0fc6c400c3ed5371.css\",\"precedence\":\"next\",\"crossOrigin\":\"\"}]],[\"$\",\"$L4\",null,{\"buildId\":\"ibMnxLVRNd6eQkSmhgFst\",\"assetPrefix\":\"\",\"initialCanonicalUrl\":\"/blog/dolphin-nautilus-titan-vs-polaris-9650iq-sport\",\"initialTree\":[\"\",{\"children\":[\"blog\",{\"children\":[[\"slug\",\"dolphin-nautilus-titan-vs-polaris-9650iq-sport\",\"d\"],{\"children\":[\"__PAGE__?{\\\"slug\\\":\\\"dolphin-nautilus-titan-vs-polaris-9650iq-sport\\\"}\",{}]}]}]},\"$undefined\",\"$undefined\",true],\"initialHead\":[false,\"$L5\"],\"globalErrorComponent\":\"$6\",\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"html\",null,{\"lang\":\"en\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"body\",null,{\"className\":\"d-flex flex-column min-vh-100\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"nav\",null,{\"className\":\"navbar navbar-expand-lg navbar-light bg-light\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"container\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L7\",null,{\"href\":\"/\",\"className\":\"navbar-brand d-flex align-items-center\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"style\":{\"width\":\"160px\",\"height\":\"90px\",\"position\":\"relative\",\"marginRight\":\"10px\"},\"children\":[\"$\",\"img\",null,{\"src\":\"/images/ThePoolLab.png\",\"alt\":\"The Pool Lab Logo\",\"style\":{\"width\":\"100%\",\"height\":\"100%\",\"objectFit\":\"contain\"}}]}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"d-none d-sm-inline\",\"children\":\"The Pool Lab\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"button\",null,{\"className\":\"navbar-toggler\",\"type\":\"button\",\"data-bs-toggle\":\"coll